IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ha-housing`
IMPORT `ha-qa`

-- Housing Act 1980 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (ha-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and every
-- situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for every role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error
-- ("it is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value
-- that makes it not hold and every later input ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. For the buyer and the tenant
-- (the baseline's seat) the answer is also asserted equal to the baseline export's own answer on the same facts. For
-- the lender the answers are worked by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts: the baseline's fixtures, copied (Jake's apartment, k074, with the baseline's ASSUMED eligibility, deposit,
-- gazetted sums, rates and rent). Expected values are written by hand from the deposited text, never copied from the
-- output. The mechanical cases at the end are generated by the scratchpad script gen_ha.py from the layer's own @export
-- list.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked way of buying` IS A `How I am buying`
ASSUME `an unasked applicant` IS AN Applicant
ASSUME `an unasked purpose` IS A `Purpose of the loan`
ASSUME `an unasked lender` IS A Lender
ASSUME `an unasked sale` IS A `What the Authority would sell me`

`as buyer` MEANS `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help`
`as tenant` MEANS `I rent, or want to rent, a home from the Housing Authority`
`as lender` MEANS `I am a bank or other institution lending to a home buyer`

`a Part IV loan` MEANS `with a loan from the Housing Authority (Part IV)`
`a Division 4 purchase` MEANS `buying a house or land from the Housing Authority itself (Part III Division 4)`
`another lender's loan` MEANS `with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender`

§§ `Fixtures (the baseline's, copied)`

`Jake, 35, single, within the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` MEANS Applicant WITH
    `meets the Authority's eligibility conditions for this kind of help (policy)` IS TRUE
    `the house is to be a home for me and my family` IS TRUE

`Jake, over the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` MEANS Applicant WITH
    `meets the Authority's eligibility conditions for this kind of help (policy)` IS FALSE
    `the house is to be a home for me and my family` IS TRUE

`Jake, within the income conditions, buying to let out` MEANS Applicant WITH
    `meets the Authority's eligibility conditions for this kind of help (policy)` IS TRUE
    `the house is to be a home for me and my family` IS FALSE

§§ `For the person buying or building a home`

-- s 15(1): an application for housing or financial help for housing must be dealt with (k074).
#ASSERT `Must the Housing Authority deal with my application, as I ask it` `as buyer` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must the Housing Authority deal with my application, as I ask it` `as buyer` FALSE EQUALS no

-- ss 35-38: Jake buying his apartment to live in, within the income conditions (ASSUMED): yes; over them, or buying to
-- let, no; land from the Authority (s 37) or an alteration the Authority thinks justified (s 38) for anyone.
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority lend to me for this, as I ask it` `as buyer` `Jake, 35, single, within the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` `to buy a house and its land` FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority lend to me for this, as I ask it` `as buyer` `Jake, over the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` `to buy a house and its land` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority lend to me for this, as I ask it` `as buyer` `Jake, within the income conditions, buying to let out` `to buy a house and its land` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority lend to me for this, as I ask it` `as buyer` `Jake, over the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` `to buy land from the Authority to build a house on` FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority lend to me for this, as I ask it` `as buyer` `Jake, over the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` `to alter or add to my house to meet local laws or for comfort` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority lend to me for this, as I ask it` `as buyer` `Jake, over the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` `to alter or add to my house to meet local laws or for comfort` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority lend to me for this, as I ask it` `as buyer` `Jake, 35, single, within the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` `some other purpose` FALSE EQUALS no

-- s 40(1): $382,200 against an ASSUMED $400,000 limit, then $300,000.
#ASSERT `Would this loan keep me within the Minister's limit, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Part IV loan` 0 382200 400000 EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Would this loan keep me within the Minister's limit, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Part IV loan` 0 382200 300000 EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Would this loan keep me within the Minister's limit, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Part IV loan` 20000 382200 400000 EQUALS no

#ASSERT `What security must I give for a Part IV loan, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Part IV loan` EQUALS `the answer is` "a first or second mortgage to the Authority over the land and its improvements, and any further security the Authority requires"

-- ss 33(6), 42(3): the gazetted standard rate, ASSUMED 6.25%.
#ASSERT `What interest rate will I pay, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Part IV loan` 6.25 EQUALS `percent a year` 6.25
#ASSERT `What interest rate will I pay, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Division 4 purchase` 5.5 EQUALS `percent a year` 5.5

-- s 46: Jake's off-the-plan apartment, deposit paid, cannot borrow the rest unaided, building $300,000 against an
-- ASSUMED $350,000, then $250,000.
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority guarantee my borrowing, as I ask it` `as buyer` `another lender's loan` `Jake, 35, single, within the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` TRUE TRUE TRUE 300000 350000 EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority guarantee my borrowing, as I ask it` `as buyer` `another lender's loan` `Jake, 35, single, within the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` TRUE TRUE TRUE 300000 250000 EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority guarantee my borrowing, as I ask it` `as buyer` `another lender's loan` `Jake, 35, single, within the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` TRUE TRUE FALSE 300000 350000 EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority guarantee my borrowing, as I ask it` `as buyer` `another lender's loan` `Jake, over the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` TRUE TRUE TRUE 300000 350000 EQUALS no

-- s 47: every approval in place, yes; the lender not approved by the Minister, no.
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority subsidise the interest on my loan, as I ask it` `as buyer` `another lender's loan` `Jake, 35, single, within the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority subsidise the interest on my loan, as I ask it` `as buyer` `another lender's loan` `Jake, 35, single, within the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority subsidise the interest on my loan, as I ask it` `as buyer` `another lender's loan` `Jake, 35, single, within the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no

-- k074: the Act says nothing about Keystart.
#ASSERT `What does the Housing Act decide about my loan, as I ask it` `as buyer` `Keystart or another company` EQUALS `the answer is` "nothing: the Act does not name Keystart; its lending policy is not law and is an input"
#ASSERT `What does the Housing Act decide about my loan, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a lender approved for an interest subsidy under s 47` EQUALS `the answer is` "only whether the Authority may subsidise the interest (s 47); the loan terms are the lender's"

-- s 31: buying from the Authority the house I or my partner rented: the rent may be credited.
#ASSERT `Can my rent be credited towards the price I pay the Authority` `as buyer` `a Division 4 purchase` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can my rent be credited towards the price I pay the Authority` `as buyer` `a Division 4 purchase` FALSE EQUALS no

-- ss 32, 33(1): terms for an eligible buyer of a house, or anyone buying land; cash only for an ineligible buyer of a
-- house; not Division 4 for what the Authority does not hold.
#ASSERT `On what terms can the Housing Authority sell me this, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Division 4 purchase` `Jake, 35, single, within the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` `a house and land held by the Authority` EQUALS `the answer is` `for cash or on terms of payment the Authority thinks fit`
#ASSERT `On what terms can the Housing Authority sell me this, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Division 4 purchase` `Jake, over the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` `a house and land held by the Authority` EQUALS `the answer is` `for cash only`
#ASSERT `On what terms can the Housing Authority sell me this, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Division 4 purchase` `Jake, over the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` `land held by the Authority, to build a house on` EQUALS `the answer is` `for cash or on terms of payment the Authority thinks fit`
#ASSERT `On what terms can the Housing Authority sell me this, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Division 4 purchase` `Jake, within the income conditions, buying to let out` `a house and land held by the Authority` EQUALS `the answer is` `not a sale under Division 4`

-- s 34(1): $382,200 unpaid against an ASSUMED $400,000.
#ASSERT `Would the unpaid price stay within the Minister's limit, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Division 4 purchase` 382200 400000 EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Would the unpaid price stay within the Minister's limit, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Division 4 purchase` 410000 400000 EQUALS no

-- s 68: hardship accepted, yes; not, no.
#ASSERT `Can I be given more time to pay on my loan or purchase` `as buyer` `a Part IV loan` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can I be given more time to pay on my loan or purchase` `as buyer` `a Division 4 purchase` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no

-- ss 72, 73: a Part IV loan or a Division 4 sale.
#ASSERT `Can the Authority pay my duty and add it to what I owe, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Part IV loan` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Authority pay my duty and add it to what I owe, as I ask it` `as buyer` `a Division 4 purchase` EQUALS yes

§§ `For the person who rents, or wants to rent, from the Housing Authority`

#ASSERT `Must the Housing Authority deal with my application, as I ask it` `as tenant` TRUE EQUALS yes

-- s 28: an eligible person; or, with the Minister's consent, an essential worker who cannot find housing.
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority rent me a house, as I ask it` `as tenant` `Jake, 35, single, within the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority rent me a house, as I ask it` `as tenant` `Jake, over the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority rent me a house, as I ask it` `as tenant` `Jake, over the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority rent me a house, as I ask it` `as tenant` `Jake, over the Authority's income conditions, buying his home` FALSE TRUE EQUALS no

-- s 30: ASSUMED $400 a week less a $150 rebate; a rebate as large as the rent leaves nothing.
#ASSERT `How much rent must I pay, as I ask it` `as tenant` TRUE 400 150 EQUALS amount 250
#ASSERT `How much rent must I pay, as I ask it` `as tenant` TRUE 100 150 EQUALS amount 0

#ASSERT `Can my rent be credited towards buying the house I rent` `as tenant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can my rent be credited towards buying the house I rent` `as tenant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can my rent be credited towards buying the house I rent` `as tenant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no

#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority house me in specialised housing, as I ask it` `as tenant` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority house me in specialised housing, as I ask it` `as tenant` FALSE EQUALS no

#ASSERT `Can I be given more time to pay my rent` `as tenant` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can I be given more time to pay my rent` `as tenant` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can I be given more time to pay my rent` `as tenant` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS no

§§ `For a bank or other institution lending to a home buyer`

-- s 46: Jake's facts from the lender's side: yes; the borrower over the income conditions, buying to let, or the house
-- over the gazetted value, no.
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority guarantee this borrower's loan from us` `as lender` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 300000 350000 EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority guarantee this borrower's loan from us` `as lender` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 300000 350000 EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority guarantee this borrower's loan from us` `as lender` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 300000 350000 EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority guarantee this borrower's loan from us` `as lender` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 400000 350000 EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority guarantee this borrower's loan from us` `as lender` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 300000 350000 EQUALS no

-- s 47: payments go to an approved lending institution, for an approved person's mortgage loan, with the Minister's
-- approval.
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority pay us an interest subsidy` `as lender` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority pay us an interest subsidy` `as lender` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority pay us an interest subsidy` `as lender` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority pay us an interest subsidy` `as lender` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Housing Authority pay us an interest subsidy` `as lender` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS no

§§ `For the buyer and the tenant: the answer equals the baseline export's`

#ASSERT `Must the Housing Authority deal with my application, as I ask it` `as buyer` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Must the Housing Authority deal with my application` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Must the Housing Authority deal with my application, as I ask it` `as tenant` FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Must the Housing Authority deal with my application` FALSE)
